    "text": "In the naming of complex ion ligands are named first alphabatically followed by name of metal ion along with its oxidation number.<h2 class=\"_2tazz\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-size: 18px; background-image: initial; background-position: 0px 0px; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; line-height: 1.4; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); letter-spacing: -0.36px; overflow: auto hidden; font-family: Karla;\">&nbsp;</h2><div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\"><span class=\"inline_editor_value\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\">the ligands are Amine and Chloride. Since there are&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-size: 1em; background: 0px 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: inherit; font-stretch: normal; font-family: KaTeX_Main, &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; line-height: inherit; text-rendering: auto; position: relative;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"katex-html\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\"><span class=\"base\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: relative; display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; width: min-content;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\">4</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;amine groups we’ll name it as tetramine and&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-size: 1em; background: 0px 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: inherit; font-stretch: normal; font-family: KaTeX_Main, &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; line-height: inherit; text-rendering: auto; position: relative;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"katex-html\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\"><span class=\"base\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: relative; display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; width: min-content;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\">2</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;chloride groups will be named as dichloro.&nbsp; Also, we have platinum metal as the central metal atom in a cation, and it’s oxidation state is&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-size: 1em; background: 0px 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: inherit; font-stretch: normal; font-family: KaTeX_Main, &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; line-height: inherit; text-rendering: auto; position: relative;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"katex-html\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\"><span class=\"base\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: relative; display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; width: min-content;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\">+</span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\">4</span></span></span></span>.</span></div><div style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\"><p class=\"ui_qtext_para\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\">Now for the other (anionic part):</p><p class=\"ui_qtext_para\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\">Here the ligand is chloride. Since there are&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; font-size: 1em; background: 0px 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: inherit; font-stretch: normal; font-family: KaTeX_Main, &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; line-height: inherit; text-rendering: auto; position: relative;\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"katex-html\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\"><span class=\"base\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: relative; display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; width: min-content;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px; position: static;\">4</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;chlorides so we’ll call it tetrachloride</span><b style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\">.</b><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; outline: 0px; background: 0px 0px;\">&nbsp;We have the central metal atom as platinum again, but since it is in the anionic coordination sphere.</span></p></div>",
